  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nIssued 408 AM MDT TUE AUG 25 2026\nA ridge will remain over the Four Corners region through\nSaturday. Tropical Storm Iselle is forecast to weaken and\nportions of the remnants will get ingested into the southwest\nflow aloft off the CA coast and move over southwest Idaho and\nextreme SE Oregon on Friday afternoon. Magic Valley precipitable\nwaters reach the 98th percentile with this feature so heavy rain\nwill be a threat with storms that form across the southwest ID\nhighlands, central ID mountains and southern Twin Falls County.\nA cold front will interact with this moisture and enhance\nthunderstorm development on Friday afternoon. This moisture \nwill be quick to move through however and clears the area by \nearly Saturday morning with dry and cooler conditions \nthereafter. Temperatures will be near normal Friday and Saturday\nbefore cooling to below normal Sunday and Monday as a trough\npasses by to the north. Temperatures rebound to near normal\nTuesday with west-southwest flow.",
